    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/da62b3e0-798b-433e-8411-41446aae02ef-image.png\" style=\"width: 322px; height: 70px;\" /></p><p>Rosenmund Reduction:&nbsp;&nbsp;The Rosenmund reduction is a reaction where acid chlorides are converted into aldehydes by employing hydrogen gas over palladium poisoned by barium sulfate.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/62593bd6-4405-4a43-a275-d30c14bf0116-image.png\" style=\"width: 352px; height: 157px;\" /></p><p>Hoffmann Bromamide reaction</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/bccf0a7d-37be-4326-8fd2-f089c97e6217-image.png\" style=\"width: 383px; height: 61px;\" /></p><p>Clemmenson reduction</p>",
